r, the KOF '96 tournament was an overwhelming commercial success. A few months after, the event triggered a fighting craze and various large corporations, expressing interest in the fad, offered to sponsor subsequent tournaments, leading to a demand for an eagerly awaited KOF '97. The fad reached all over the globe and in no time KOF '97 came into being.", "summary": "The King of Fighters '97 is a 1997 fighting game produced by SNK for the Neo Geo arcade and home console. It is the fourth game in The King of Fighters series. It was ported to the Neo-Geo CD, as well as the PlayStation and the Sega Saturn in Japan only.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/the-king-of-fighters-97", "videos": [{"id": 10104, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "-x53X0d3YMo", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-x53X0d3YMo", "title": "THE KING OF FIGHTERS'97 Trailer", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/-x53X0d3YMo/maxresdefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 854, "name": "The King of Fighters"}]}